{"metadata":{"description":"A starter template for DeepSeek Harness (dsh) plugins: six plugin shapes, fourteen browser UI surfaces, and demo slash commands in one installable bundle.","id":"gh:1334717694","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-plugin-template","slug":"kun2-5code/dsh-plugin-template","topics":["cordis","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","plugin","template","typescript"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"A starter template for DeepSeek Harness (dsh) plugins: six plugin shapes, fourteen browser UI surfac"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"es, and demo slash commands in one installable bundle."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-plugin-template"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"A ready-to-run, ready-to-install starter template for DeepSeek Harness (`dsh`) plugins. It demonstra"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"tes the most common plugin shapes in one minimal installable bundle:"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"- **Config** — a `Config` interface plus a Schemastery schema whose live fields carry `.volatile()`,"},{"id":"p5s2","text":" so the Plugins page can edit them without a restart (docs)
- **Tool** — `ctx.tools.register(defineT"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"ool(...))` registers a model-callable tool with a `card`-tagged render intent (docs)
- **Events** — "},{"id":"p5s4","text":"`ctx.on` / `ctx.emit` with declaration merging for typed events (docs)
- **Service** — a class-form "},{"id":"p5s5","text":"plugin that provides a service to other plugins (docs)
- **Hook** — a `tools/pre-execute` permission"},{"id":"p5s6","text":" gate that denies tool calls by config (docs)
- **Browser half (client)** — `src/client/` registers "},{"id":"p5s7","text":"browser UI on **fourteen surfaces** (index: docs/ui-surfaces.md): a **configuration form** on the Pl"},{"id":"p5s8","text":"ugins page, a **sidebar footer action**, an **input dock** strip above the composer, a **shell overl"},{"id":"p5s9","text":"ay**, a **header utility** badge, **input tool-row buttons** (left/right), a custom **command row** "},{"id":"p5s10","text":"for `/dsh-demo`, a **General settings row**, a **Plugins settings tab**, a **settings header action*"},{"id":"p5s11","text":"*, a **session header action**, a **composer dock** strip, and **per-message actions** on AI replies"},{"id":"p5s12","text":" — plus a `presentResult` render intent on the `greet` tool."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"The template follows the official bundle distribution model: the package declares `dsh.bundle` plus "},{"id":"p6s2","text":"`cordis.patch.yml`, and `dsh plugin add` activates it as a config layer."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Directory structure"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"### Install as a bundle (for users)"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"From any directory, install this package (or your fork) into a dsh profile:"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"A GitHub install pulls **source**; pnpm runs `prepare` (i.e. `tsdown`) to build `lib/`. On pnpm ≥10 "},{"id":"p13s2","text":"the first git-dependency prepare is refused; add the package name pnpm prints to the profile's `pnpm"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"-workspace.yaml` and retry:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"> This allowlist authorizes executing that package's code at install time — only allow source you tr"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"ust, and prefer pinning a commit: `github:you/dsh-plugin-template#<sha>`."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Verify the config layer and boot:"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"> Note: a custom-named profile (e.g. `demo`) contains only `dsh-base` and is **headless** (no GUI).
"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"> For the Web GUI and the configuration form below, use the `web` profile (`= dsh-base` + `dsh-web-a"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"pp`) — see testing the form."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"### Local development (modifying the plugin)"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"From the root of a deepseek-harness source checkout, load this repo's source directly via an overlay"},{"id":"p20s2","text":" (no install, no build):"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Set `name` in `dev/cordis.yml` to this repo's path on your machine as a **`file://` URL**, open `htt"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"p://127.0.0.1:3080`, and ask the model to call the `greet` tool. A bare absolute path fails on Windo"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"ws: the Loader hands an entry's `name` straight to `import()`, and `D:\…` parses as protocol `d:`, s"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"o the row dies with `ERR_UNSUPPORTED_ESM_URL_SCHEME` and the plugin never loads. Produce the URL wit"},{"id":"p22s5","text":"h `node -e "console.log(require('node:url').pathToFileURL('<path>').href)"`."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"> A `--patch` overlay only loads the plugin's **host half** (module resolution cannot reach package-"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"level declarations).
> To test the browser half you must install into a profile (resolved by `name: "},{"id":"p23s3","text":"dsh-plugin-template`) — see the next section."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Run the checks yourself during development:"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"`typecheck` runs `tsc` over the source, the tests, and the build config. `test:unit` runs the vitest"},{"id":"p26s2","text":" specs; `smoke` runs against `lib/`; `test` runs all of it in that order."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"> If this repo sits INSIDE a `deepseek-harness` checkout (nested, as in the harness repo root), `pnp"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"m install` is captured by the parent workspace and installs nothing here — the template is not a wor"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"kspace member. Use `pnpm install --ignore-workspace` so the template installs its own `node_modules`"},{"id":"p27s4","text":" from its own lockfile; or clone the template standalone."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"### Testing the configuration form (in the GUI)"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"The form renders in the browser and depends on dsh's client-modules discovering the `dsh.client` dec"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"laration **by package name**, so the package must be installed into a profile (a `--patch` source pa"},{"id":"p29s3","text":" package name**, so the package must be installed into a profile (a `--patch` source path won't do):"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"Open `http://127.0.0.1:3080`, go to the **Plugins** page in the sidebar, and select **Plugin Templat"},{"id":"p31s2","text":" `http://127.0.0.1:3080`, go to the **Plugins** page in the sidebar, and select **Plugin Template**:"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"1. The bundle's page renders a configuration form with `greeting`, `maxRetries`, and `verbose`;
2. C"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"hange `greeting` and click **Save** — the deployment accepts the values and the status line reports "},{"id":"p32s3","text":"success;
3. Back in a session, ask the model to call the `greet` tool — it uses the new greeting (th"},{"id":"p32s4","text":"e host half reads `config.greeting.get()` on every call, no restart);
4. The change lands in the set"},{"id":"p32s5","text":"tings document under `$DSH_HOME` and survives restarts. **Reset to default** clears the field so it "},{"id":"p32s6","text":"re-inherits the value from `cordis.patch.yml`."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"There is no allowlist to edit and no restart step: a plugin entry whose `Config` has at least one `."},{"id":"p33s2","text":"volatile()` field is served automatically, and the Plugins page passes this page its `form` (accepte"},{"id":"p33s3","text":"d values plus a revision-fenced `mutate`)."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"After editing the client half (`src/client/`), rerun `pnpm build` and refresh the page (the client b"},{"id":"p34s2","text":"undle's rev query cache-busts)."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"## Making it your own plugin"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"1. Rename the package: keep `package.json` `name` (npm name, e.g. `dsh-my-plugin`), `src/index.ts` `"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"name`, and `cordis.patch.yml` `id`/`name` consistent. **Renaming also touches browser-half spots:** "},{"id":"p36s3","text":"the client bundle `id` in `tsdown.config.ts` (`__ModuleLoader__.load({ id })`), `NAMESPACE` in `src/"},{"id":"p36s4","text":"client/constants.ts`, `dsh.client.inject` in `package.json`, and `NAMESPACE` in `src/client/constant"},{"id":"p36s5","text":"s.ts` (the Plugins page keys off it), plus `locale/en.json`. When renaming the `./service` subpath, "},{"id":"p36s6","text":"update `exports`/`files` too.
[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"## How the browser half works"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}
